  recipeId: safety
  concept: 'Authored objective: Verify the 64-sample ground-stand envelope.

    Authored
    requirement: Prove spin-up, gust recovery, descent, overcurrent cut and emergency
    stop on the stand.

    General teaching principle: Protection logic must be
    verified under both normal and fault conditions, including reset and recovery
    behavior.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this
    objective is complete.'
  analogy: A safety lock must prevent unintended activation even when the normal
    switch would permit it.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Passing a normal-operation test is not proof that the protection
    system responds correctly to faults.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Verify the 64-sample ground-stand envelope\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Verify the 64-sample ground-stand envelope\u2019, what result
    or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 123, perform the objective \u2018Verify the 64-sample ground-stand
    envelope\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against:
    Prove spin-up, gust recovery, descent, overcurrent cut and emergency stop on
    the stand.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not
    grade your answer."
